---
source: crates/slopvac/tests/testing_toolkit.rs
expression: "help.replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\").replace(\"slopvac.exe\", \"slopvac\")"
---
Lint prose and source comments. `slopvac PATH...` lints, as does `slopvac lint PATH...`.

Exit codes: 0 pass, 1 a gate failed, 2 the run was incomplete or the invocation was invalid.

Usage: slopvac [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  lint         Lint prose and source comments. Bare paths run this command.
  explain      Explain a rule.
  rules        List rules.
  init         Write a commented slopvac.toml and set up agent steering.
  doctor       Check the binary, configuration and pack health.
  self         Manage this installation.
  lsp          Run the language server on standard input and output.
  migrate      Migrate a 2.x project to 3.0: config, inline directives and steering blocks
  terms        Manage project terms
  genre        Print the genre of each file, with scores and the reasons for the choice
  validate     Check config, front matter and inline directives without linting
  setup        Install or remove project-local steering for a harness
  prime        Print guidance for agents, one topic at a time
  completions  Print a shell completion script.
  man          Write man pages.
  plugins      Manage plugins and packs: sync, trust, update.
  packs        List installed rule packs.
  onboard      Print the agent onboarding text.
  reference    Generate or check the rules reference.
  report       Preview or submit an issue report.
  review       Run the prose reviewer on files.
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --offline
          Never use the network. SLOPVAC_OFFLINE=1 and `[network] offline = true` do the same, and nothing turns it off.

      --color <WHEN>
          Colour output. NO_COLOR is honoured.
          
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --no-color
          Alias for --color never.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
